"""rt-sim -- [RT_SIM_V1] the demo's simulated world: Teams, Hospitals, Ambulances, Fire, Power, Victims and Boats in the
Seattle metro area, Vashon included (John, 2026-11-01: "Pre-populate the RAM with some instances ... using simulated GPS
data"; "The ambulances, teams, and victims move around the map in real time"; "Don't exclude water. Boats may be first
responder transports").

Each simulated instance is its own writer of its own truth, as a real device is (PLAN.md, the 2026-11-01 decision),
on a session of its own (fnw1), with own=True, so its cells go with it ([OWNED_CELL_GOES_WITH_THE_SESSION_V1]):
  (rt-who, <mission>, <id>)   latest  {name, kind, team, color, host:"", station:""}   presence
  (rt-pos, <mission>, <id>)   latest  {name, kind, team, color, lat, lng, at, status, ...}   where it is now
in RangerTrak's general RAM, wherever FDF_VAR/app-where.json says it is served now. Moving instances write their
position every TICK seconds; when the RAM is another one (relocated), every instance opens its session there and
writes its truth again, at once. A victim delivered to a hospital leaves: its session ends and it is gone from every
map. rt-sim stopped: every instance is gone. Ambulances say what they do to everyone, (rt-msg, <mission>, <id>.<ms>);
team members now and then say something to their team, (rt-team, <mission>, <id>.<ms>) in the team's own RAM when it
is served (rangertrak.<team>). (rt-mission, settings, <mission>) is written by this program too: the exercise is its own.

Kinds and what moves:
  team       members of four colour-coded teams, walking between nearby places of their zone
  ambulance  dispatched to a victim who needs transport, to the scene, then to the nearest hospital of its zone
  boat       fireboats and marine units on the Sound and the lakes, between water points
  victim     walking slowly; status: needs transport -> transported (and a new one appears elsewhere)
  hospital   fixed; beds available changes as ambulances arrive
  fire       fixed incidents; severity
  power      fixed outages; customers out
  host       the nodes things connect through (simulated ones, "Sim-..."); every other instance's cells say which, "via"
             (a real node's position is its own GPS sensor, metric_upsert GPS Position, read by the app)
Positions are approximate (hand-placed); this is a demo world, not a map service.

  rt-sim [--mission ID] [--tick S] [--seed N]
Environment: FDF_VAR (/opt/fdf/var), FDF_PY (the fnw1 module's directory).
"""
import argparse, json, math, os, random, sys, time

BUILD_TAG = "rt-sim-2026-11-01-r5"
LIB = os.environ.get("FDF_PY") or os.path.join(os.environ.get("FDF_HOME", "/opt/fdf"), "lib", "python")   # (it ships in the add-in)
sys.path.insert(0, LIB)
sys.path.insert(0, os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__)))   # the add-in ships fnw1.py beside this program
import fnw1  # noqa: E402

VAR = os.environ.get("FDF_VAR", "/opt/fdf/var")
WHERE = os.path.join(VAR, "app-where.json")
KEY = "rangertrak.general"
BOX = (47.30, 47.80, -122.55, -122.05)          # lat min/max, lng min/max: Seattle metro and Vashon

# places on land, by zone (approximate centres of neighbourhoods); a unit stays in its zone
